Harold thinks back on how he got here. The book, the library, and everything going black. How old was that book? Where was it from? 
->"It must have bothered someone that you found it. That’s why they trapped you here."
        “This isn’t useful.” Harold stops this dangerous train of thought. He has to try his best to keep his mind intact. 
->"What a waste of time. Escape is the only thing you should be focused on."
        <<reduce_fear "Harold Auden">>
        “This isn’t useful.” Harold stops this dangerous train of thought. He has to try his best to keep his mind intact. 
->"You fell asleep. You’ll wake up eventually."
        “This isn’t useful.” Harold stops this dangerous train of thought. He has to try his best to keep his mind intact. 
->"Maybe it gave you some disease. Some ancient parasite that laid dormant between the pages…"
        <<add_fear "Harold Auden">>
        <<discover_fear "Harold Auden" 6>>
        //Fear of Parasites
        Harold begins to itch at his skin. He convinced himself that there is something lurking beneath it. His eyes widen as he studies every inch of his body. He gets lost in a frenzy, clawing and scratching, before realizing that all of his clothes are on the floor and the only marks are from his own doing. “If there is something wrong with me, I can’t see it.” He slowly gets dressed again, continuing with the thought that something could be slowly eating away at him. 
